; prior: Python — `if "":` skips the branch (empty string is falsy).
; expectation: Loon DIVERGES: "" is a value and therefore truthy. The
; divergence is taught by E0209 on the never-falsy String condition.
; principle: diverge loudly (agent-first.md P1/P2).
; expect-stdout: empty-string-is-truthy
; expect-check: E0209
[fn main []
  [println [if "" "empty-string-is-truthy" "empty-string-is-falsy"]]]
